From 7c6b835b4749c9c94cba53cf47f05b5b6f1aa7d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maximilian Khan <maxjkh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 09:08:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] beast-rank E23: shared output basis for MoE LoRA
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

build_lora_mm_id() applied lora_b per-expert unconditionally via
ggml_mul_mat_id. This adds the shared-basis case: when lora_b is 2D
(ne[2] == 1) while the base weight is per-expert (ne[2] > 1), apply a single
output basis across all experts with a plain ggml_mul_mat instead.

That is the adapter shape the E28/E29 bytes work needs — a shared basis is
what lets rank be spent once rather than once per expert, which is where the
"-16.6% adapter bytes at tied KLD" result comes from. Without this branch the
graph builder cannot express it and shared-basis adapters simply fail to load
against an MoE base.

Developed in the .wt-e23 worktree on 2026-08-04 against 0ef6e55ed (b10254) and
left uncommitted there for 11 days — gitignored, unreachable from any branch,
and NOT captured by the beast-rank-kernels rescue on 2026-08-14, whose
llama-graph.cpp differs. Committed now as a rescue point; a patch export is
vendored in the openbeast repo under research/lowrank/kernels/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/llama-graph.cpp | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-graph.cpp b/src/llama-graph.cpp
index 9dde345df..c820c7eb4 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-graph.cpp
@@ -1539,11 +1539,20 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_lora_mm_id(
         const float rank  = (float) lw->b->ne[0];
         const float scale = alpha ? lora.second * alpha / rank : lora.second;
 
-        ggml_tensor * ab_cur = ggml_mul_mat_id(
-                ctx0, lw->b,
-                ggml_mul_mat_id(ctx0, lw->a, cur, ids),
-                ids
-                );
+        ggml_tensor * ab_cur;
+        if (lw->b->ne[2] == 1 && w->ne[2] > 1) {
+            // shared output basis: 2D lora_b applied to all experts
+            ab_cur = ggml_mul_mat(
+                    ctx0, lw->b,
+                    ggml_mul_mat_id(ctx0, lw->a, cur, ids)
+                    );
+        } else {
+            ab_cur = ggml_mul_mat_id(
+                    ctx0, lw->b,
+                    ggml_mul_mat_id(ctx0, lw->a, cur, ids),
+                    ids
+                    );
+        }
 
         ab_cur = ggml_scale(ctx0, ab_cur, scale);
         res = ggml_add(ctx0, res, ab_cur);
